   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 4,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "builded -- Cf. Exodus 33:7-11. This arrangement for worship was temporarily called the \"tabernacle.\""
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 11,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "eat and drink -- Symbol of communion. Cf. Luke 22:15-18. A blood-sprinkled people, see Hebrews 9:19-22 who had not yet broken the law could thus commune with God. Never again was this repeated. Cf. Exodus 24:9-11 with Leviticus 16:2 and Hebrews 9:6-8 But cf., under grace,; Ephesians 2:13; Hebrews 10:19,20."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
